caption: $:/tags/hypergsd/Type
title: Type tag list

! Summary
Register a new item type.

! Detail
Create a tiddler tagged `$:/tags/hypergsd/Type` with an `hgsd-type` field holding the type name (must be unique — the creation mapping keeps the first match on duplicates):

```
title: $:/GSD/Stakeholder
tags: Documentation [[HyperGSD API]]
hgsd-type: stakeholder
```

A type in this tag list automatically:

* refreshes all GSD views when its items change (the generic `hgsd-type-gate` whitelist run),
* appears in the new-item modal's Type dropdown — the tag list carries no `list` field, so the order follows the engine's tag index (shadow members in plugin load order, then ordinary tiddlers); pin a position with `list-after` or `list-before` on the type tiddler itself,
* gets its tag applied to items created with that type.

The core members are `$:/GSD/Action` and `$:/GSD/Project`; the rest ship from sub-plugins — `$:/GSD/Contact` ([[Contacts|$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd-contacts/readme]]), `$:/GSD/Reference` ([[References|$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd-references/readme]]) and `GSD/Contexts` ([[Contexts|$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd-contexts/readme]]; the dashboard tiddler itself is the member — the tag list and the type anchor are the same open `GSD/*` tag). Absent sub-plugins simply drop their member — the tag list, type dropdown and creation flow degrade cleanly.

! Best Practice
Pair a new type with an [[AfterCreation|AfterCreation]] rule if it needs side effects (back-references, status changes).